w("## 3. Family-shift validation (leave-clusters-out)")
w()
w(f"**Design (`p5_03`).** Per stage, MOFs are embedded without labels (z-score, PCA 20) and clustered with k-means (K = {FS['K']}); whole clusters go to **test** (about 20% of MOFs), other whole clusters to **calibration** (about 20%), the rest to **training**; a random forest (300 trees, fixed in advance; thermal = regressor on temperature, solvent/water = classifier, score = P(stable)) is trained on the training clusters, the per-stage split-conformal recall rule is calibrated on the calibration clusters, and recall is measured on the test clusters. Repeated {FS['R']} times (new k-means seed and cluster order). **Control:** the same models with calibration and test both drawn (random halves) from the test clusters, which are exchangeable inside the cluster. The {FS['R']} repetitions share MOFs, so they are not independent; 'share of reps >= target' is descriptive.")
w()
w("| stage | target | cluster-held-out recall, mean (sd) [min] | share of reps >= target | kept | same-cluster control recall | control share >= target |")
w("|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
for st in ("thermal", "solvent", "water"):
    df = pd.DataFrame(FS["results"][st])
    for a in FS["alphas"]:
        g, c = df[f"recall_{a}"], df[f"ctrl_recall_{a}"]
        w(f"| {st} | {1 - a:.2f} | {g.mean():.3f} ({g.std():.3f}) [{g.min():.3f}] | {np.mean(g >= 1 - a):.2f} | {df[f'kept_{a}'].mean():.3f} | {c.mean():.3f} | {np.mean(c >= 1 - a):.2f} |")
w()
dfs = {st: pd.DataFrame(FS["results"][st]) for st in ("thermal", "solvent", "water")}
w("Context per stage (means over repetitions): " + "; ".join(f"{st}: test MOFs {d.n_test.mean():.0f}, test AUC {d.auc_test.mean():.3f}, mean kNN distance to training MOFs calibration {d.dist_cal.mean():.1f} vs test {d.dist_test.mean():.1f}" for st, d in dfs.items()) + ".")
w()
sh = {st: [d[f"recall_{a}"].mean() - (1 - a) for a in FS["alphas"]] for st, d in dfs.items()}
w("**Result: the plain rule falls short under cluster shift, mostly for thermal.** Mean shortfall (realised recall minus target, over the four targets): " + "; ".join(f"{st} {min(v):+.3f} to {max(v):+.3f}" for st, v in sh.items()) + f". The spread across repetitions is large (sd up to {max(d[[f'recall_{a}' for a in FS['alphas']]].std().max() for d in dfs.values()):.2f}) and only about half of the repetitions reach the target even for the control, as expected for a marginal guarantee. The same-cluster control sits at the target, so the shortfall comes from the calibration-to-test shift and not from the code. The size of the shortfall depends on how clusters are formed (here k-means in a PCA of the released features, K = {FS['K']}); I did not vary K or the embedding.")
w()
w("### Distance-aware variant (`p5_04`)")
w()
w(f"Because the plain rule fell short, I implemented one distance-aware (Mondrian) variant, **fixed before looking at its results**: statistic = mean distance to the {DA['knn']} nearest training MOFs (z-scored features, training statistics); {DA['n_bins']} bins with edges at the calibration terciles; one split-conformal threshold per bin from the calibration positives in that bin. Same splits and models as above (the plain results were recomputed and asserted equal). **No coverage proof is claimed under cluster shift**; within each bin the usual argument needs calibration and test MOFs of that bin to be exchangeable, which the cluster shift violates.")
w()
w("| stage | target | plain recall mean (sd) | plain kept | distance-aware recall mean (sd) | distance-aware kept | paired change in recall (mean) | share of reps >= target: plain / dist-aware |")
w("|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|")
for st in ("thermal", "solvent", "water"):
    df = pd.DataFrame(DA["results"][st])
    for a in DA["alphas"]:
        p, q = df[f"plain_recall_{a}"], df[f"mond_recall_{a}"]
        w(f"| {st} | {1 - a:.2f} | {p.mean():.3f} ({p.std():.3f}) | {df[f'plain_kept_{a}'].mean():.3f} | {q.mean():.3f} ({q.std():.3f}) | {df[f'mond_kept_{a}'].mean():.3f} | {np.mean(q - p):+.3f} | {np.mean(p >= 1 - a):.2f} / {np.mean(q >= 1 - a):.2f} |")
w()
dd = {st: np.mean([np.mean(pd.DataFrame(DA['results'][st])[f'mond_recall_{a}'] - pd.DataFrame(DA['results'][st])[f'plain_recall_{a}']) for a in DA['alphas']]) for st in ("thermal", "solvent", "water")}
w("**Result: the distance-aware variant does not help.** Mean paired change in recall over the four targets: " + "; ".join(f"{st} {v:+.3f}" for st, v in dd.items()) + ". For thermal, where the shortfall is largest, it lowers recall further; for solvent it is mixed and for water it changes recall by less than 0.01. Plausible reasons (not tested): the shift is not mainly a distance-to-training effect (in solvent and water the test clusters are even closer to the training MOFs than the calibration clusters, see the context line), and splitting the calibration positives into three bins adds threshold noise. I stopped after this one pre-specified variant because trying more on these clusters would be tuning on the test clusters. Untried: weighted conformal prediction with estimated density ratios, cluster-level (group) calibration, a larger calibration set drawn from many clusters.")
w()
w("## 4. The cascade claim and the sensitivity of the 17")
w()
w("**Wording now used.** Each stage's conformal guarantee is for that stage's own stable MOFs. It does **not** imply the same miss probability for the MOFs that are stable at all three stages, so 'recall >= 1 - alpha for MOFs stable at all three stages' holds under an **assumption**, not as a proved property. The 17 all-stable MOFs cannot test the assumption, and their out-of-fold scores are lower than those of the other stage-stable MOFs for thermal and water (`notes/review.md` H3). The observed cascade recall (0.94-0.98 on the 17) is consistent with the target but does not confirm it. Simulation (review S7c): if the all-stable MOFs are 0.5 sd 'harder' in every stage, the union-bound cascade's recall is 0.78 at target 0.90.")
w()
