w("- The SI's solvent and water numbers are reproduced by retraining on the SI's own split (solvent only with the as-coded early-stopping behaviour); thermal R2 0.41 is not. For solvent and water the earlier 'paper vs release' discrepancy is explained by which split was used; for thermal it is not (R2 0.41 remains unreproduced, cause unknown).")
w("- Those SI numbers come from a test set where about half of the MOFs have a same-group MOF in training, and the group-clean half scores much lower (section 1d).")
w("- The plain conformal recall rule is valid for exchangeable calibration/test MOFs but falls short under cluster shift; the one distance-aware variant tried does not fix this. The stacked-filter recall guarantee holds only under assumptions that were not met in the shift experiment (section 3) and are untestable for the all-stable population (section 4).")
w("- The group-vs-random gap is robustly positive but its size is a distribution, not a number (section 5).")
